.TH EUCLID-CLI-EDS-PUT-RECORD 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.3.2" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eds-put-record \- write the records of one type at one name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eds put-record
.BR \-\-zone | \-z
.I ZONE
[\fB\-\-name\fR|\fB\-n\fR \fINAME\fR]
.BR \-\-type | \-t
.I TYPE
.BR \-\-value | \-v
.I VALUE
[\fB\-\-value\fR \fIVALUE\fR...]
[\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes a record set \- every record of one type at one name \- and
replaces the one that was there.
.PP
.B It replaces rather than adds.
To add a third address to a name that has two, give all three.
To remove one, give the other two. Replacing the set in one write means
the server never answers with half the old addresses and half the new
ones.
.PP
Every value is checked before anything is stored, so a value the server
could not serve is refused here rather than skipped later.
.PP
The server answers the new records within a moment. Resolvers that
cached the old ones keep them for up to their TTL.
.SH TYPES AND VALUES
Values are written as in a zone file, without the quoting. A value with
spaces in it is one argument to the shell, so quote it.
.TP
.B A
An IPv4 address:
.IR 192.0.2.1 .
.TP
.B AAAA
An IPv6 address:
.IR 2001:db8::1 .
.TP
.B CNAME
The name this one is an alias of:
.IR api.corp.example .
Exactly one value. A CNAME has to be the only record at its name, and
the zone's apex cannot be one, since it holds the zone's SOA and NS.
Both are refused rather than stored.
.TP
.B MX
Preference and mail host:
.IR "10 mail.corp.example" .
.TP
.BR NS ", " PTR
A host name.
.TP
.B SRV
Priority, weight, port and host:
.IR "10 5 8080 api.corp.example" .
The host must be a name with an address record, never an address.
.TP
.B TXT
Any text, up to 4000 bytes. Longer than 255 bytes, it is sent as
several strings, which a reader joins together.
.PP
SOA cannot be written: each zone's SOA is made from the zone itself.
.SH NAMES
.TP
.I api
relative to the zone;
.TP
.IR api.corp.example " or " api.corp.example.
fully qualified;
.TP
.IR @ " or no " \-\-name
the zone's apex;
.TP
.I *.dev
a wildcard, answering for every name below
.I dev.corp.example
that has no records of its own.
.PP
A name outside the zone is refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-zone " " \fIZONE\fR
The zone's apex. Required.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
The record's name, as above. Defaults to the apex.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
.BR A ,
.BR AAAA ,
.BR CNAME ,
.BR MX ,
.BR NS ,
.BR PTR ,
.B SRV
or
.BR TXT ,
in any case. Required.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-value " " \fIVALUE\fR
A value. Repeat for several. At least one is required.
.TP
.BR \-\-ttl " " \fISECONDS\fR
How long resolvers may cache the records. Defaults to the zone's TTL.
.SH OUTPUT
The record set as stored, as JSON:
.IR zone ,
.I name
(fully qualified),
.IR type ,
.IR ttl ,
.IR values ,
.I created
and
.IR modified .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The record set was written.
.TP
.B 1
No such zone in your account, a value that cannot be encoded, a name
outside the zone, a type that cannot be stored, a CNAME beside other
records or other records beside a CNAME (HTTP 409), or a grant does not
allow it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eds put-record -z corp.example -n api -t A \e
    -v 10.1.2.3 -v 10.1.2.4
euclid-cli eds put-record -z corp.example -n www -t CNAME -v api.corp.example
euclid-cli eds put-record -z corp.example -t MX -v "10 mail.corp.example"
euclid-cli eds put-record -z corp.example -n _ldap._tcp -t SRV \e
    -v "0 5 389 dc1.corp.example"
euclid-cli eds put-record -z corp.example -t TXT -v "v=spf1 -all"
euclid-cli eds put-record -z corp.example -n "*.dev" -t A -v 10.9.0.1 --ttl 30
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eds (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-list-records (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-delete-record (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-get-answer (1)
